From 1ae3fd991be6809aaa42a2383b8fe2e58a585632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:28:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] attest: the fork's mock TEE and mock attested CA out of the
 tree

attest.go carried the proof of concept's mock TEE: its Evidence format
(a COSE_Sign1 EAT under a mock provider key), the code that made such
Evidence and the code that appraised it. internal/mockca/attest.go
carried the mock Verifier, Credential Authority and Secret Vault that
used them. Nothing else used either, and the server no longer builds the
mock CA (0009). Both go, with the dependencies only they needed
(veraison/eat, go-cose and theirs); the comments that spoke of the mock
now say what the code does. internal/mockca keeps GlobalSign's mock CA
for the upstream tests that use it; the server does not import it.

The proof of concept's container encryption (EncECDHP256,
SealCredentialBundle) stays: it is the container type of the
AttestationCA interface. The TACRA backend forwards the Secret Vault's
hpke-auth container unchanged (RawRetriever).
---
 attest.go                 | 247 +--------------
 go.mod                    |   9 -
 go.sum                    |  22 --
 internal/mockca/attest.go | 637 --------------------------------------
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 911 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 internal/mockca/attest.go

